                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. Romero to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-12-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 21, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: I have the honor to remit to you
                    various articles from the principal daily papers of Paris, published during the
                    late days of November last, in which there is very ably discussed the important
                    question, Who is the responsible party, in France, for the ill results which the
                    Mexican adventure has had? The semi-official press treats of throwing the
                    responsibility on the opposition and on public opinion, while the independent
                    journals attribute it to the Emperor Napoleon.</p>
                <p>I gladly avail of this opportunity, sir, to repeat that I am, very respectfully,
                    your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M. ROMERO.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">WilliAM H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>








